---
// Destination: src/pages/terms.astro
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Terms of Use | Enterprise Agile"
  description="Terms of use, content licensing, and intellectual property notice for this site."
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
  <main id="main-content" class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-wrap">

      <header class="legal-header">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">
          Effective date: <time datetime="2026-08-18">18 August 2026</time>
        </p>
        <p class="legal-intro">
          By visiting this site you agree to these terms. They are short, fair, and written
          in plain language.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section aria-labelledby="site-purpose">
        <h2 id="site-purpose">1. Purpose of this site</h2>
        <p>
          This site is a professional portfolio belonging to <strong>Kranthi Kumar
          Nagulapally</strong>, an independent enterprise program leader. Its purpose is
          to share delivery frameworks, professional experience, and published thinking
          with the enterprise agile and program management community.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="content-license">
        <h2 id="content-license">2. Content license — what you may do</h2>
        <p>
          All <strong>written content</strong> on this site — including frameworks,
          methodology descriptions, case study narratives, articles, and any other
          original text — is published under the
          <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
          </a> licence.
        </p>
        <p>Under CC BY 4.0 you are free to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Share</strong> — copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format.</li>
          <li><strong>Adapt</strong> — remix, transform, and build upon the material for any purpose, including commercially.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Under the following conditions:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Attribution</strong> — you must give appropriate credit, provide a link to
            this site, and indicate if changes were made. A clear attribution such as
            "Originally published by Kranthi Kumar Nagulapally at [site URL]" satisfies this
            requirement.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>No additional restrictions</strong> — you may not apply legal terms or
            technological measures that legally restrict others from doing anything the licence
            permits.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="code-license">
        <h2 id="code-license">3. Source code license</h2>
        <p>
          The <strong>source code</strong> for this site (Astro components, scripts,
          configuration files, and Worker code) is available at
          <a href="https://github.com/nagulapallikranthi/enterprise-agile-site" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            github.com/nagulapallikranthi/enterprise-agile-site
          </a>
          and is published under the
          <a href="https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MIT Licence</a>.
          You may use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
          copies of the source code without restriction, subject to retaining the original
          copyright notice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="no-ai-training">
        <h2 id="no-ai-training">4. AI training restriction</h2>
        <p>
          The written content on this site (frameworks, articles, case studies) is original
          intellectual property. You may <strong>not</strong> use this content as training
          data for commercial AI or machine learning models without explicit written
          permission. This restriction applies regardless of any other licence terms above.
        </p>
        <p>
          To request permission for AI training use, contact
          <!-- TODO: Replace with your professional email after domain registration -->
          <a href="mailto:nagulapalli.kranthi@gmail.com">nagulapalli.kranthi@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="accuracy">
        <h2 id="accuracy">5. Accuracy and professional advice</h2>
        <p>
          The frameworks, case descriptions, and methodologies on this site represent the
          site owner's professional opinion and experience. They are shared for educational
          and illustrative purposes and do not constitute professional advice for your
          specific situation. Apply any framework with appropriate judgement and adaptation
          for your context.
        </p>
        <p>
          Quantitative outcomes described on this site (delivery improvements, cost
          reductions, etc.) reflect real professional delivery results and are generalised
          to protect employer and client confidentiality. They are not independently
          verified and should be understood as indicative rather than audited figures.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="external-links">
        <h2 id="external-links">6. External links</h2>
        <p>
          This site may link to external sites (LinkedIn, GitHub, Cloudflare, etc.).
          These links are provided for convenience. The site owner is not responsible
          for the content, privacy practices, or accuracy of any external site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="changes">
        <h2 id="changes">7. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may be updated at any time. The effective date above reflects the
          most recent revision. Continued use of the site after an update constitutes
          acceptance.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="contact">
        <h2 id="contact">8. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For any question about these terms, licensing, or permissions:
          <!-- TODO: Replace with your professional email after domain registration -->
          <a href="mailto:nagulapalli.kranthi@gmail.com">nagulapalli.kranthi@gmail.com</a>
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    min-height: 100vh;
    padding: 80px 8% 120px;
  }
  .legal-wrap { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .legal-header { margin-bottom: 56px; padding-bottom: 32px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12); }
  .legal-header h1 { font-size: clamp(36px,5vw,56px); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -1.5px; line-height: 1.08; margin: 16px 0 14px; }
  .legal-meta { color: var(--brand-silver); font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .legal-intro { font-size: 18px; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.75; max-width: 680px; }
  section { margin-bottom: 44px; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(20px,2.5vw,26px); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.5px; margin-bottom: 14px; padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); }
  p { color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 14px; max-width: 720px; }
  ul { margin: 12px 0 16px 24px; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  li { color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; }
  a { color: var(--brand-azure); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  a:hover { color: white; }
</style>
